Current 12:02 tree, after the bit4 split: the remaining A32 stops in my corpus are only two words:

1) `asr r0,r0,r1` = e1a00150 (also e1a01152) reaches `if (op2 == 5u) return n2a32_arm_media;`. QADD/QSUB are only bits[27:23]==00010; DP register-shift has bits[27:23]==00011. Gate it:
     if (((insn >> 23) & 0x1Fu) == 0x02u && op2 == 5u) return n2a32_arm_media;
   (same for the SMLAxy group if you keep the op2==8/A/C/E form; your exact 0x0F900FF0/0x0F900090 masks are equivalent and safer).
2) `ldrh r2,[r0,#-2]` = e15020b2 still goes to arm_dp because the extra-load test requires bits24-23==11 and this is P=0,U=1 (01). Use the nibble test independent of bits24-23:
     if ((insn & 0x90u) == 0x90u) {
         unsigned lo = (insn >> 4) & 0xFu;
         if (lo == 0xBu || lo == 0xDu || lo == 0xFu ||
             (lo == 0x9u && ((insn >> 8) & 0xFu) == 0xFu))
             return n2a32_arm_mem;
     }
   Keep the `op2==9 -> arm_dp` multiply line after it.

With just those two edits on top of the current tree (plus V17/V18-V20 stubs), arm-O0 executes all 86 non-VFP kernels with 0 mismatches; VFP stops at ee000a10. I have the patched copy at /tmp/n2hw-T01/exp2/core_fix7.c if you want to diff it (not in the tree).
